<title>UK: LIFFE white sugar ends firmer, above $300.</title>
<headline>LIFFE white sugar ends firmer, above $300.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>London's spot white sugar contract managed to end above $300 on Friday but traders said sellers may be quick to take profits from another upside assault.</p>
<p>Covering of short positions accounted for a lot of the market's firmness during the early part of the session when March hit $300 a tonne, touching off buy stops.</p>
<p>March last traded at $303.60, up $3.90.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7729</p>
